{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JvBShc6ESsL8m7c4ywS77g","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel05.1-uc002-unexpand\n     2→title: \"Convert spaces to tabs via unexpand\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator runs the Go unexpand binary on one or more files or stdin. By default the\n     6→  binary converts only leading whitespace runs to tabs where alignment permits; with -a it\n     7→  converts all whitespace runs in the line. The differential testing harness then runs\n     8→  both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gunexpand from coreutils) with\n     9→  identical inputs and confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n    10→\n    11→actor: Human Operator\n    12→\n    13→trigger: |\n    14→  The operator has completed the PRD (prd025-unexpand.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n    15→  a passing differential test for cmd/unexpand.\n    16→\n    17→flow:\n    18→  - id: F1\n    19→    step: |\n    20→      The operator runs the Go unexpand binary on a file or stdin.\n    21→      Example: printf '        text\\n' | ./bin/unexpand\n    22→  - id: F2\n    23→    step: |\n    24→      cmd/unexpand reads each input character, tracking the current column position. In\n    25→      default mode it processes only leading whitespace. With -a it processes all whitespace\n    26→      runs throughout the line.\n    27→  - id: F3\n    28→    step: |\n    29→      When a run of spaces exactly reaches a tab stop, cmd/unexpand replaces the run with\n    30→      one or more tab characters. Spaces that do not reach a tab stop are kept as spaces.\n    31→  - id: F4\n    32→    step: |\n    33→      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/unexpand and\n    34→      gunexpand with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n    35→  - id: F5\n    36→    step: |\n    37→      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n    38→      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n    39→  - id: F6\n    40→    step: |\n    41→      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n    42→      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n    43→\n    44→touchpoints:\n    45→  - T1: \"cmd/unexpand — space-to-tab conversion, leading vs. all-whitespace mode, custom tab stops (prd025-unexpand R1, R2, R3)\"\n    46→  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n    47→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n    48→\n    49→success_criteria:\n    50→  - id: S1\n    51→    criterion: cmd/unexpand compiles and ./bin/unexpand exists after mage build.\n    52→  - id: S2\n    53→    criterion: The differential test for default mode passes; leading 8 spaces become a tab, non-leading spaces are unchanged.\n    54→  - id: S3\n    55→    criterion: The differential test for -a passes; all runs of spaces at tab-stop boundaries are converted throughout the line.\n    56→  - id: S4\n    57→    criterion: The differential test for partial space runs (not reaching a tab stop) passes; spaces are preserved.\n    58→  - id: S5\n    59→    criterion: The differential test for -t N passes; spaces are converted at multiples of N columns.\n    60→\n    61→out_of_scope:\n    62→  - unexpand is not a lossless inverse of expand for all inputs; the asymmetry is intentional.\n    63→  - Unicode multi-column character width is not tested; LC_ALL=C is used.\n    64→\n    65→test_suite: test-rel05.1\n    66→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8da431a-575c-43a7-97e5-a163d19babfc","uuid":"f3de40c6-de5a-4ac7-ab9f-85227d4c8177","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/352/docs/specs/use-cases/rel05.1-uc002-unexpand.yaml","content":"id: rel05.1-uc002-unexpand\ntitle: \"Convert spaces to tabs via unexpand\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator runs the Go unexpand binary on one or more files or stdin. By default the\n  binary converts only leading whitespace runs to tabs where alignment permits; with -a it\n  converts all whitespace runs in the line. The differential testing harness then runs\n  both the Go binary and the Homebrew reference binary (gunexpand from coreutils) with\n  identical inputs and confirms that their outputs are identical byte-for-byte.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD (prd025-unexpand.yaml) and invokes do-work to produce\n  a passing differential test for cmd/unexpand.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs the Go unexpand binary on a file or stdin.\n      Example: printf '        text\\n' | ./bin/unexpand\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      cmd/unexpand reads each input character, tracking the current column position. In\n      default mode it processes only leading whitespace. With -a it processes all whitespace\n      runs throughout the line.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      When a run of spaces exactly reaches a tab stop, cmd/unexpand replaces the run with\n      one or more tab characters. Spaces that do not reach a tab stop are kept as spaces.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The differential testing harness (pkg/testutils) executes both ./bin/unexpand and\n      gunexpand with the same stdin, args, and environment.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The harness compares stdout byte-for-byte with no normalization. Both binaries must\n      produce identical output bytes and exit codes.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      If the outputs match, the test passes. If they diverge, the harness reports the\n      triggering args, both outputs, and both exit codes.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"cmd/unexpand — space-to-tab conversion, leading vs. all-whitespace mode, custom tab stops (prd025-unexpand R1, R2, R3)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/testutils — RunDiffTests, binary execution and byte-for-byte comparison\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler for graceful SIGPIPE handling\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: cmd/unexpand compiles and ./bin/unexpand exists after mage build.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: The differential test for default mode passes; leading 8 spaces become a tab, non-leading spaces are unchanged.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: The differential test for -a passes; all runs of spaces at tab-stop boundaries are converted throughout the line.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: The differential test for partial space runs (not reaching a tab stop) passes; spaces are preserved.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: The differential test for -t N passes; spaces are converted at multiples of N columns.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - unexpand is not a lossless inverse of expand for all inputs; the asymmetry is intentional.\n  - Unicode multi-column character width is not tested; LC_ALL=C is used.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel05.1\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
